WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.360
It's true what Larkin says about
parents, they do mess you up.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.640
They don’t mean to - usually.
But they do.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.920
By the time I'm eight, Dad's mania
and anxiety are kicking in,

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.240
and that, mixed with a newfound
fervour for Christianity,

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.400
makes things lively.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.480
By age 11, bedtime stories are out
and tales of hell fire are in.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.560
According to Dad,
me and everyone I know

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.560
are going to suffer eternal agony
unless we turn to Jesus.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.000
Ah man,

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.520
I could save myself...

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.680
what about all the people on TV?

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.880
All the players on Match of the Day?

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.600
Would I have to wait
in the car park after games?

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:44.880
"Mr Cantona...

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.200
kicking people is a sin.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.360
Yes, even if they
do support Crystal Palace."

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.200
By now Dad is relentless.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.960
And the panic attacks are regular.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.160
Running around the house,
screaming, delirious.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:58.960
And things deteriorate.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.800
By 12, 13, I'm crying constantly.
Struggling to get out of bed.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.240
And by 14, I'm starving myself.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.720
At 15 I have to have
a year off school

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.560
and be treated at a psychiatric ward.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.400
Complex PTSD is a variation
of post-traumatic stress disorder.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:19.800
We associate that with people
affected by specific incidents.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.920
In war or after an assault
or car crash.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:26.400
The complex variety refers to those
who endured repeat abuse

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.080
usually at the hands of care-givers.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.800
It may have been a religious parent,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.720
a violent parent, one that drank,
sexually abused you,

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:36.200
scapegoated, shamed
or just ignored you.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:41.600
One common sign of complex PTSD
is an intensely critical inner voice

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.240
that just won't get off your back.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.520
You know the one,
that says things like:

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.880
"You're useless.
You've achieved nothing."

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.640
One negative thought will kick in and
then they'll all come out to play.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.080
"Oh and you look rubbish naked."

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.360
"Oh by the way, everybody hates you."

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.800
"I can't believe you just stood on
that snail, and you like snails."

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.320
Another sign is flashbacks

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.160
and these are often more subtle
than specific memories.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.560
The situation you're in now will
remind you, even subconsciously,

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.480
of a time that you felt overwhelmed.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.720
For me it's social gatherings.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.640
When I walk into a room I often feel
like I'm about to be humiliated.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.720
So my fight-flight instinct
kicks in hard.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.240
At parties, I'll often go
to the bathroom several times

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:25.440
just to feel calm.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.520
I love bathrooms.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.080
Sitting on the bath

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:31.200
listening to the party downstairs.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.680
[muffled party conversations]

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.880
I practice bathroom sound effects too

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.240
like the sound a toilet roll makes
when you pull off the last sheet.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.920
After that I'm okay for a bit.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:47.920
But then someone new
will come up and say:

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.360
"Hello, I'm Ted!"

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.640
I'll get all adrenalised
and just leave.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.960
There is no danger but the psyche
doesn’t know the difference.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.880
That's complex PTSD in a nutshell.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:02:59.640
Sorry Ted.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:04.520
Other signs are depression,
substance abuse, isolating yourself

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:05.960
and avoiding relationships.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.960
You may have no clue
why you feel any of this.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:10.640
But there is help.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.320
Self-help books are
a great place to start,

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.720
especially if you're nervous
about therapy or talking to a friend.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:18.880
Therapy's been great too.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:21.840
Someone to talk to,
help join the dots,

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.160
give names to things.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.000
I also try and stay healthy
and clear headed.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.880
Vegan diet, exercise and meditation.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.480
And of course stand-up.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.120
Talk about facing your fear
of humiliation.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:37.040
I did get to make some peace with my
Dad before he died a few years ago.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.160
A tumour on the brain.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.600
Felt strangely right for a man
so lost in his own mental chaos.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:48.200
I did love him, he meant well,
he was just negligent and confused

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:49.440
and it caused damage.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.080
It's important to know
where the blame lies.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:55.840
These feelings aren’t your fault
and it can be helped.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:00.720
So see it like you see any injury -
listen to it, give it what it needs.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.120
And remember it’s okay to feel bad

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.880
but fear, anxiety, anger, depression
ruin all of the good stuff.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.760
All of the fun.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:10.840
And this

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.800
is supposed to be fun.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:23.600
Thanks for watching. 
Don’t forget to subscribe! :)

